/target/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.orig
*.bak
target/
node_modules/
_build/
deps/
.elixir_ls/
.cache/
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
dist/
/dist/
/out/

# `build/` is NOT ignored: in the RSR root shape it is the tracked build-
# orchestration directory (just/ phase modules, container/, guix/manifest).
# Build OUTPUT for this workspace is `target/`, listed above. If a tool ever
# writes artefacts under build/, ignore that specific subpath here rather than
# the whole directory — ignoring build/ hides the canon directory and makes
# `git add build/...` a silent no-op.

# Site builds generated by .github/workflows/casket-pages.yml and pages.yml.
# They are produced in CI only; ignoring them stops a local `just docs-site`
# from presenting untracked output as root-shape drift.
/_site/
/site/
/.casket-ssg/
/.ddraig-ssg/

# Session dispatch artefacts: .github/../session/dispatch.sh writes
# .session/LAST-CANONICAL-COMMAND.md (and local-hooks.log) into the repo it is
# run against. Per-session scratch, never canonical text — and left untracked it
# would read as root-shape drift the next time anyone ran the gate.
.session/

# Claude Code project state (checkpoints, history) — created by the tool
# itself, never committed. CLAUDE.md is the tracked instruction file and lives
# at the repository ROOT (the generator, pre-commit and Claude Code all read
# it from there), not inside this directory.
/.claude/
